post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
==> trunk runs as the user trunk, with its data in /var/lib/trunk. To start:
      sudo -u trunk trunk user add NAME -admin -data /var/lib/trunk
      sudo systemctl enable --now trunk
    It listens on 127.0.0.1:8420; /usr/share/doc/trunk-photos/Caddyfile puts it behind Caddy.
==> trunk-ai (content search, faces) needs onnxruntime; see /usr/lib/systemd/system/trunk-ai.service.
MSG
}
